                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[u]Relatable Premise[/u]\n\nA young adult otome visual novel set in Japan that follows Yuka Kishimoto, a high school senior experiencing her final week of school. As graduation approaches, Yuka and her friends face important choices involving love, friendship, life, and their futures. The decisions she makes in these final days can shape how Yuka remembers this important period of her life. Total completion time can be as little as 59 minutes.\n\n[u]Life Lessons[/u]\n\nThe narrative explores themes of finding conviction, living a fulfilling life, embracing haziness, confusion, and uncertainty, and discovering that life is more than school, exams, college, and education.\n\n[u]Meaningful Dialogue[/u]\n\nMost of the dialogue is thought-provoking, including “Remember that... sometimes you have to go through a period of your life doing something you don’t really like to find out what you really love. The trade off is worth it.” “It’s what I think, but no matter what I want you to make decisions for yourself. Obviously listen to what your teachers and peers say, but also make your own decisions. Not knowing what you want to do with your life is ok. Not knowing what college you want to go to is ok.” “It’s good you're thinking about these things. I found that even though there is agony in the dream I am chasing, I am way happier in chasing that dream than any of the dreams that society expected. Chasing dreams feels edgy because we know we can get hurt, but it's that rush of getting closer and closer... it’s so addictive.” and “That’s part of it really. I soon realized that there were some things out of my power and control and I began to care less and get angrier less. I learned to just calm down and just try to enjoy life however possible.”\n",
